Umbra was one of the [[Titans]] of [[Casterwill]]'s [[Elder son of Casterwill|first son]]. This Titan was found by [[Hernán Cortés]]. His [[Amulet]] remained in Cortés' tomb, guarded by another Titan, [[Conquistador]], and a magic barrier. {{source|Gremlow Infestation!}} The [[Pied Piper]] of Hamelin's magic flute was used to control the guardian Titan, which then deactivated the barrier. Later, Umbra bonded with [[Dante Vale]]. Umbra's power was then used to escape from being crushed by Conquistador. {{source|The Power of Umbra}}

His teleportation power was only able to be used a few times, so Dante used [[Copykind]] to be able to use Umbra's power again to reach the [[castle of Vlad Dracul]] without weakening the Titan. {{source|Lok's Leadership}}

Umbra later transported Lok, Sophie, Dante, and Den to the [[Spiral Mark]] to stop the [[Nullifiers]]. {{Source|Words from Eathon}} Umbra then played a small, but crucial, role in preventing the return of the Nullifiers by transporting Dante and [[Phoenix]] up to the [[Red Comet]]. {{Source|The Spiral Mark}} After stopping the Red Comet, a weakened Umbra teleported back to the Spiral Mark and jumped on the Betrayer, saving the Huntik team. With the last of his energy, he transported back Dante's ashes, endowed with the ability of Phoenix, before collapsing and permanently fading away.{{Source|Dante's Return}}
